{
 "_about": "The type system of the CapCut build (capcut/typeset.py, references/typography.md). A timeline's \"type\" in capcut.json names a style; without one the style follows the ad's format (\"by_format\"). Each style sets, per on-screen line, the typeface, size hierarchy, colour, the one emphasis, the placement and the finish. Fonts are CapCut library fonts (resource id + file); a font CapCut has not downloaded falls back to the sans with a NOTE. Sizes are CapCut text sizes at segment scale 2. y is the canvas height from -1 (bottom) to 1 (top); safe area: text stays between y -0.52 and 0.70 (Reels and Feed UI cover the top 15% and the bottom 24%) and inside x +-0.86. Line 1's three parts are [subject, linking words, tension word(s)]: the first on its own line, the other two after it; \"case0\": \"upper\" sets the first part as a small tracked label. A \"numbered\" style shows Lines 2-4 as 1/2/3 above each reason (list). \"layout\": \"stagger\" on Line 3 sets its first half to the left and the second below it to the right (\"edge\", default 0.8, is how far out they reach); \"italic\": true on a line slants the sans.",
